<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21437" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īlĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a poetical name of</i> Rhea Silvia, <i>daughter
				of Numitor and mother of Romulus and Remus</i>, Enn. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Charis. p. 70</span></i> P. (Ann. v. 56
			Vahl.); <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1, 274</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2,
				383</span></i>; <i><span class="en">598</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				2, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 9, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">4, 8,
			22</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īlĭădes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>son of Ilia.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Romulus Iliades Iliadesque Remus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 4, 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pater,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Romulus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					4, 23</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fratres,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Romulus and Remus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.
					3, 62</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Subst., i. e. <i>Romulus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14,
				781</span></i> and 824.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
